  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention: Emerging and Zoonotic Infectious Diseases - International Health Regulations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing emerging infectious diseases and international health regulations. U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), National Center for Emerging and Zoonotic Infectious Diseases (NCEZID) works with partners around the world to prevent illness, disability, and death caused by a wide range of infectious diseases - from the rare but deadly, like anthrax and Ebola, to the more common, like foodborne disease and healthcare-associated infections.</narrative>
  </description>
